# Byte-deterministic fixtures must keep LF line endings on every platform, so a
# committed golden file never gets CRLF-rewritten on checkout (autocrlf) and then
# byte-mismatches the adapter's LF output. Applies to the hermetic adapter fixtures.
fixtures/adapters/** text eol=lf

# Historical estimator artifacts are verified by SHA-256 over exact committed
# bytes.  Keep their JSON and Markdown payloads LF-only on Windows checkouts so
# the integrity record hashes the same content users actually execute against.
build/estimators/** text eol=lf

# WSL bootstrap scripts must remain executable Bash with LF endings even when
# the repository is checked out by Git for Windows with autocrlf enabled.
scripts/foundation/*.sh text eol=lf

# Historical journal segments are byte-addressed archival payloads. Preserve LF
# bytes and suppress heuristic whitespace/diff rewriting of exact boundaries.
docs/research/neurips-2026-workshop/execution-journal/*.md text eol=lf -diff

# The adversarial-review fixture declares a SHA-256 over the exact committed
# bytes of each reviewed input. `digest_file` is deliberately byte-exact, since
# a review attests to the precise bytes that were reviewed, so a CRLF checkout
# would make every declared digest stale. Commit c069c0d did exactly that: it
# "refreshed" the spec from a CRLF working copy and broke the fixture on every
# LF checkout. Pin the endings instead of weakening the digest.
fixtures/adversarial_review/** text eol=lf

# Governed research evidence is hashed over exact canonical JSON bytes and must
# survive native Windows checkout without a CRLF rewrite.
docs/research/neurips-2026-workshop/evidence/**/*.json text eol=lf
